From: VyOS LS1046A Build <build@vyos.io>
Date: Sun, 6 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] debug(ask2): 0148 — log KG scheme EKFC/MV during setup
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LS1046A Mono Gateway DK hardware-specific]
Risk-Tier: C

Add pr_info in keygen_scheme_setup to log the exact EKFC, match vector,
hash control, and FQ base values written to hardware for each scheme.
This definitively answers whether the default RSS schemes get
DEFAULT_HASH_KEY_EXTRACT_FIELDS (0x00180206) or 0x00000000 for EKFC.

Temporary debug patch — remove after KG extraction verified.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_keygen.c
@@ -552,6 +552,9 @@ int keygen_scheme_setup(struct fman_keygen *keygen, u8 scheme_id,
 	if (scheme->use_hashing) {
 		/* configure kgse_ekfc */
 		scheme_regs.kgse_ekfc = DEFAULT_HASH_KEY_EXTRACT_FIELDS;
+		pr_info("ASK2-DBG scheme%u hashing: ekfc=0x%08x mv=0x%08x hc=0x%08x fqb=0x%08x\n",
+			scheme_id, scheme_regs.kgse_ekfc,
+			scheme_regs.kgse_mv, scheme_regs.kgse_hc, scheme_regs.kgse_fqb);
 
 		/* configure kgse_ekdv */
 		tmp_reg = 0;
